# ODS-LEONES — AI Stack Server

## Objective

Use ODS as the reference integration for the **AI Stack Server** profile.

LEONES provides preflight, consent, orchestration, validation and measurement. ODS provides the AI stack.

## Relevant capabilities

ODS combines local inference, Open WebUI, gateways, RAG/search, voice, agents/workflows, image generation, privacy and observability. Documented components include llama-server, Open WebUI, LiteLLM, Qdrant, SearXNG/Perplexica, Whisper/Kokoro, Hermes Agent, n8n, APE, OpenCode, ComfyUI, Dashboard, Privacy Shield, Token Spy and Langfuse.

## Evolution

### From model selection to real capability selection

ODS should move beyond reducing selection to “which model fits this GPU?”. The target question is:

> **Which inference configuration produces the best real capability on this GPU, for this workload and policy?**

The decision object is an **Inference Profile** combining hardware, model, quantization, runtime, kernel, context, KV cache, MTP/speculative decoding, vision, slots, reasoning effort, flags and evidence.

The external Bonsai 2 research demonstrates why: the same GPU and weights can move from ~26 tok/s to ~40 tok/s through a specialized kernel and to ~50 tok/s with MTP; context limits also change by VRAM tier. LEONES keeps these figures as external evidence until physical reproduction.

See: [Bonsai 2 / small-GPU — external experimental evidence](Bonsai2-Small-GPU-EXTERNAL-EVIDENCE-eng.md).

### Boundary contract

LEONES provides prediction, experiment design, benchmarking and evidence. ODS provides execution, orchestration and runtime selection/composition. The loop is: LEONES → ODS → physical inference → measurement → LEONES.

The integration should evolve toward a capability registry and adaptive runtime selector instead of assuming a single inference engine.

**Classification:** primary ODS/LEONES integration.